-- title:
--   Adapted smooth ambient coordinates at a point of a permissible centre
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a discrete valuation ring (a domain) with a chosen $\pi \in R$ generating its maximal ideal, let $A$ be an $R$-algebra of finite type, and let $J \subseteq A$ be an ideal containing the image of $\pi$, with $A/J$ carrying an algebra structure over the residue field $k = R/\mathfrak m_R$ compatible with its $R$-algebra structure. Let $\mathfrak p$ be a prime of $A$ and $\mathfrak q$ a prime of $A/J$ whose preimage under $A \to A/J$ is $\mathfrak p$. Assume that $A/J$ is smooth over $k$ at $\mathfrak q$, and that the point $\mathfrak q$ of $\operatorname{Spec}(A/J)$ lies in the free locus of the $(A/J)$-module $(A/J) \otimes_A \Omega_{A/R}$. Then there are $g \in A$ with $g \notin \mathfrak p$, natural numbers $r, n$, and a commutative ring $C$ (in the same universe) equipped with an $R$-algebra structure and an algebra structure on $A_g =$ `Localization.Away g` over $C$, compatible with the $R$-structures, such that: $C$ is smooth over $R$ (formally smooth and of finite presentation); the structure map $C \to A_g$ is surjective; and there exist $y : \mathrm{Fin}\,r \to C$, $z : \mathrm{Fin}\,n \to C$ together with a basis of $\Omega_{C/R}$ indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\,r \sqcup \mathrm{Fin}\,n$ given by the differentials $d y_i$ and $d z_j$, for which the preimage in $C$ of the ideal generated by $J$ in $A_g$ equals $(\pi, z_1, \dots, z_n)$, and the $n$ elements $1 \otimes d(\text{image of } z_j)$ of $\bigl(C/(\pi, z)\bigr) \otimes_C \Omega_{A_g/R}$ are linearly independent over $C/(\pi, z)$.
--
--   This is the coordinate-normalisation step in the study of dilatations along a permissible centre: after shrinking around $\mathfrak p$, $\operatorname{Spec} A_g$ is realised as a closed subscheme of a smooth affine $R$-scheme $\operatorname{Spec} C$ whose module of differentials is free on $dy_1, \dots, dy_r, dz_1, \dots, dz_n$, with $(\pi, z_1, \dots, z_n)$ cutting out the centre. It is used in the bound on the smoothness defect of an affine dilatation at a point where the centre is smooth and the restricted differentials are free.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Algebra_exists_smooth_surjective_localizationAway_basis_kaehlerDifferential_comap_eq_span.lean

import Mathlib

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
